# Development from source: copy to `.env`, start the dependencies
# (`docker compose up -d`), then `npm run dev`.

PORT=4870
PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:4871

DATABASE_URL=postgres://folio:folio@localhost:5490/folio
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6390

# Encrypts saved git tokens and personal AI keys at rest (AES-256-GCM, see
# server/secretCrypto.ts). The value below is fine for local development; a
# REAL DEPLOYMENT MUST SET ITS OWN unique secret (`openssl rand -hex 32`) —
# anyone who knows it can decrypt every saved credential in the database.
# Without it, saving a credential is refused with a clear error instead of
# storing plaintext. Do not change it later: already saved credentials would
# stop decrypting.
FOLIO_SECRET=dev-only-folio-secret-change-in-production

# Prefilled into the create-space dialog's repository field. May point at a
# brand-new empty repository. Optional; users can type any other URL.
# FOLIO_DEFAULT_REPO_URL=https://gitlab.example.com/your-org/folio-data

# Where uploaded files live: local | s3
ASSET_BACKEND=local
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9100
# S3_BUCKET=folio-assets
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=folio
# S3_SECRET_KEY=folio-minio-dev
# S3_REGION=us-east-1

# "Sign in with Google" (server/auth/google.ts). The button appears only when
# both the client id and secret are set. GOOGLE_ALLOWED_DOMAINS is a
# comma-separated allowlist of email domains; when it is empty, Google
# sign-in lets nobody in.
# Redirect URI to register: <PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=example.com

# Public-demo mode (server/demo.ts). OFF by default — an ordinary instance
# never serves any of this. When on, the login screen shows a "Public demo —
# sign in as…" block with the accounts below, a thin banner shows in the app,
# and a demo account is barred from creating API tokens and changing passwords.
# The demo passwords are PUBLIC by design: they are handed out only while the
# mode is on, and never logged. The accounts themselves must already exist
# (seed them); this only advertises them.
# FOLIO_DEMO_MODE=1
# A JSON array, or a path to a file holding one:
# FOLIO_DEMO_ACCOUNTS=[{"email":"editor@demo.example","password":"demo-password","name":"Dana Editor","role":"Editor","description":"Editor in Engineering and Product"}]
# How often the operator resets the demo data; shown to visitors (optional).
# FOLIO_DEMO_RESET_HOURS=6
# In demo mode ONLY, these are switched off for everybody (403 "disabled in the
# public demo"): API tokens, the AI assistant and AI keys, git/Confluence
# endpoints that connect to a caller-chosen host (/api/git/*, creating a space,
# connect-git, /api/import/*, saved git/Confluence credentials), share links,
# invites, and changing name/username. A demo account also cannot change a
# password. Uploads are capped:
# FOLIO_DEMO_MAX_UPLOAD_MB=5
# /mcp and OAuth limits, demo mode ONLY (server/demoLimits.ts; in process memory,
# per request.ip, so set TRUST_PROXY behind a proxy). 429 + Retry-After + a JSON-RPC error.
# Requests per minute per user+IP on /mcp (a failed login counts per IP):
# FOLIO_DEMO_MCP_RPM=60
# Writing tool calls (readOnlyHint=false) per hour per IP:
# FOLIO_DEMO_MCP_WRITES_PER_HOUR=100
# Fixed, not configurable: /mcp body 1 MiB, one write's arguments 200 KiB,
# POST /oauth/authorize and POST /oauth/token 30/min per IP.

# Behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Traefik, Caddy), request.ip is the proxy's
# address for every visitor, and the login rate limit (10/min per IP) becomes
# one shared bucket for everybody. TRUST_PROXY=true makes the app believe the
# client address the proxy reports in X-Forwarded-For — but only from a proxy on
# a loopback/private address (same host, or the docker network), and only the
# entry the proxy appended, never one a client forged. Also accepted: a
# comma-separated list of proxy addresses/CIDRs. A bare hop count ("1") is
# refused. Unset = no proxy: the TCP peer is the client (the safe default when
# the port is reachable directly).
# TRUST_PROXY=true

# AI assistant (Cursor SDK). Each user normally connects a personal Cursor API
# key in their account settings (stored encrypted with FOLIO_SECRET).
# CURSOR_API_KEY is an optional operator-level fallback for everyone. The
# runtime needs Node.js >= 22.13; on older Node the assistant reports itself
# unavailable and the rest of Folio keeps working.
# CURSOR_API_KEY=

# Default model for new assistant conversations ('auto' lets Cursor choose).
CURSOR_AGENT_MODEL=auto

# Per-conversation workspace and the SDK's own state. Default: subfolders of
# the data directory.
# CURSOR_AGENT_WORKSPACE_ROOT=
# CURSOR_AGENT_STATE_DIR=

# Deadlines for one assistant run, in milliseconds: Ask mode, Agent mode, and
# the idle limit (no activity at all from the SDK).
CURSOR_AGENT_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
CURSOR_AGENT_TIMEOUT_MS_AGENT=1800000
CURSOR_AGENT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
